  "readPublishedPolicy": "Read the published document",
  "legalDraftNotice": "This summary is a draft. The developer must publish and approve the complete legal documents before subscriptions are available.",
  "privacyPolicyBody": "Your selected screenshots, extracted text and collections are processed on this device and stored in app-private storage. No screenshot or OCR content is sent to a backend or AI provider. Automatic sync is optional and requires separate Photos access; you can change access in device Settings.\n\nOptional Pro subscriptions use Apple/Google and RevenueCat. After you choose to connect, a purchase identifier and purchase history are shared to validate subscriptions. SDK diagnostics and automatic attribution-identifier collection are disabled. RevenueCat provides purchase reporting for the developer. We add no advertising, tracking or app analytics SDK.\n\nDelete individual entries or use Delete Imported Screenshot Data in Settings to remove imported entries, copies and import history. Manual entries remain until you delete them. Original Photos are never deleted. Temporary processing copies are removed after each attempt or swept on the next launch after interruption. Purchase records are retained separately by the store and RevenueCat; deleting local screenshots does not cancel a subscription or erase records they must retain.\n\nUninstalling can remove local data. The app requests iOS file protection and backup exclusion for its database and imported copies; previous backups and filesystem snapshots may retain data. Sensitive-screen checks can miss content and deletion is not certified secure erasure. External saved links open only when you choose. No user account is required. If you choose Google or Apple sign-in, Firebase Authentication and the selected provider process your sign-in identity (UID, optional name/email or Apple relay email, credentials and connection metadata). We do not send screenshots or OCR text to them. SDKs manage session credentials; they are not saved in the app database. Firebase UID is used for RevenueCat identity after billing consent. Delete Account requires reauthentication, deletes the Firebase account and clears this device’s session while keeping its local collections. Store and RevenueCat purchase records are separate; subscriptions are not cancelled by account deletion. No screenshot cloud backup or cross-device collection sync exists.\n\nGoogle Sign-In and Firebase Auth may process diagnostics, device/user identifiers and usage information for their services. Their SDK privacy declarations include broader categories as well. The app does not request a phone-number or location permission; provider metadata is separate from screenshot content. No separate advertising or app-analytics service was added; we do not claim all provider operational measurements are disabled.",
  "termsBody": "Free features include selected imports, local organization, viewing, editing and deletion. On iOS, Apple Vision and local rules analyze screenshots without paid cloud AI. Android selected imports keep the image for manual organization; text recognition is currently iOS-only.\n\nAutomatic screenshot discovery is free on iOS while the app is active. Pro increases manual selection batches from 10 to 50 photos on iOS. It does not provide continuous background monitoring or unlimited cloud AI. Monthly and yearly subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled through the store at least 24 hours before renewal. The store displays the exact local price and confirms each purchase. Payment is handled by the store. Manage or cancel in your store subscription settings; deleting this app or its content does not cancel billing.\n\nExisting saved data remains accessible if Pro expires or verification is temporarily unavailable. Recently verified subscription access may continue offline for up to 72 hours, never beyond its known expiry. A refund, revocation or expiry removes the larger Pro batch allowance after verification.\n\nClassification and sensitive-content checks may be wrong. Review and edit results when needed. This draft requires developer legal approval and complete publisher/contact details before release.",
